"""Business-facing automation guide and a local, scripted email walkthrough."""


def automations_article(icon):
    return f'''<div class="doc-meta"><span class="pill gold">AUTOMATIONS</span><span>Everyday work, fewer repeated steps</span></div>
    <h2>Give REACH a task.<br>Let the steps follow.</h2>
    <p>An automation is a repeatable workflow: a series of steps that AI carries out toward a result. Instead of asking for each small action separately, describe the job, provide the right information, and tell REACH what needs your review.</p>
    <p>For a business email, that could mean finding a client’s message, understanding the request, preparing a reply, and showing it to you before sending. You give the direction; REACH helps with the work in between.</p>
    <div class="automation-use-cases" aria-label="Example business automations"><div>{icon('chat')}<strong>Customer follow-ups</strong><p>Turn a client conversation into a clear reply.</p></div><div>{icon('file')}<strong>Project updates</strong><p>Turn project notes into a progress summary.</p></div><div>{icon('users')}<strong>Meeting preparation</strong><p>Turn a brief into an agenda and questions.</p></div></div>
    <h3>Watch a business email come together.</h3>
    <p>This example follows a website studio replying to a client who is ready to move ahead. Play the chat, review the draft, then approve the <strong>simulated</strong> send.</p>
    <section class="automation-demo" data-automation-demo aria-label="Animated business email example">
      <div class="automation-demo-header"><span>{icon('mark')} REACH <span class="muted">/ Client follow-up</span></span><span class="pill gold">Illustrative example</span></div>
      <p class="automation-demo-note">Sample conversation only. No account is connected and no real email is read or sent.</p>
      <ol class="automation-track" aria-label="Email workflow"><li data-automation-phase="1"><span>1</span>Read</li><li data-automation-phase="2"><span>2</span>Draft</li><li data-automation-phase="3"><span>3</span>Review</li><li data-automation-phase="4"><span>4</span>Send</li></ol>
      <div class="automation-demo-grid">
        <div class="automation-chat"><div class="automation-pane-title">THE CONVERSATION</div><div class="automation-messages" tabindex="0" aria-label="Example conversation transcript">
          <div class="automation-bubble automation-user" data-automation-message="0"><strong>You</strong><p>Read the latest email from Maple &amp; Co. about the website refresh. Draft a friendly reply asking for their brief and preferred timing. Show me the email before sending.</p></div>
          <div class="automation-bubble" data-automation-message="1"><strong>REACH <span>Reading the conversation</span></strong><p>I found the client’s message: “We’d like to move forward with the website refresh. What do you need from us?”</p></div>
          <div class="automation-bubble" data-automation-message="2"><strong>REACH <span>Preparing the reply</span></strong><p>I’ll thank them, ask for their brief and preferred timing, and keep the next step clear.</p></div>
          <div class="automation-bubble" data-automation-message="3"><strong>REACH <span>Ready for review</span></strong><p>Your draft is ready. Review the recipient, subject, and message before approving the send.</p></div>
          <div class="automation-bubble automation-user" data-automation-message="4" hidden><strong>You <span>Simulated approval</span></strong><p>The draft looks good. Send this email.</p></div>
          <div class="automation-bubble" data-automation-message="4" hidden><strong>REACH <span>Example complete</span></strong><p>The email was sent in this simulation. No real message was sent.</p></div>
        </div><div class="automation-working" data-automation-working hidden aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span> REACH is working through the task</div></div>
        <div class="automation-mail"><div class="automation-pane-title">THE EMAIL <span data-automation-mail-status>Draft for review</span></div>
          <div class="automation-mail-empty" data-automation-mail-empty hidden>{icon('file')}<p>The email draft will appear here as REACH works through the request.</p></div>
          <div class="automation-mail-draft" data-automation-mail-draft><dl><div><dt>To</dt><dd>Jordan at Maple &amp; Co. <span class="muted">(sample client)</span></dd></div><div><dt>Subject</dt><dd>Next steps for your website refresh</dd></div></dl><div class="automation-mail-body"><p>Hi Jordan,</p><p>Thanks for confirming you’d like to move forward with the website refresh.</p><p>Could you share your project brief and preferred timing? I’ll use those details to prepare the next steps for your review.</p><p>Looking forward to working together,<br>The website team</p></div></div>
          <div class="automation-approval"><p data-automation-review-note>Review the draft before sending.</p><button class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" type="button" data-automation-approve hidden>Approve simulated send {icon('arrow')}</button></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="automation-controls" data-automation-controls hidden><div class="button-row"><button class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" type="button" data-automation-play>Play example</button><button class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" type="button" data-automation-next>Next step</button><button class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" type="button" data-automation-replay>Replay</button></div><p data-automation-status role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">Ready to play the example.</p></div>
      <noscript><p class="automation-demo-note">The transcript and draft above show the example. Enable JavaScript for playback and simulated approval.</p></noscript>
    </section>
    <h3>How to use automations in REACH.</h3>
    <ol class="automation-howto"><li><strong>Connect the tools the task needs.</strong><p>In Studio, open <strong>Settings → App Connections</strong> and connect your work account. For email, reading and sending have separate permissions. You can also start with text you paste into chat when you only need a draft.</p></li><li><strong>Describe the result in everyday language.</strong><p>Say what to work on, which information to use, and what a good result looks like. Include the tone, the recipient, and whether you want a draft or a message sent after review.</p></li><li><strong>Run the task and review the result.</strong><p>REACH uses the tools available to the conversation to work through your request. Read the proposed email and approve sending when you are ready. A connected account and permission to send are required for a real email.</p></li><li><strong>Reuse the instructions.</strong><p>When the task comes up again, use the same instructions with the new client, conversation, or project details. Start with one useful workflow and refine it as you go.</p></li></ol>
    <div class="automation-prompt"><div><h3>Try a request like this.</h3><button class="copy-btn" type="button" data-copy="automation-prompt">{icon('copy')}<span>Copy prompt</span></button></div><p id="automation-prompt">Find the latest email from [client] about [project]. Summarize what they need, then draft a friendly reply asking for [next step]. Show me the recipient, subject, and full message for review. Do not send until I approve.</p></div>
    <p class="automation-scope"><strong>When does it run?</strong> This guide shows a workflow you start in chat. Reusing a prompt does not create a recurring schedule. Scheduled or unattended work needs a separately configured scheduling setup.</p>
    <div class="docs-pager"><a class="text-link" href="#quickstart" data-doc="quickstart">Set up your first workspace {icon('arrow')}</a><a class="text-link" href="download.html">Get REACH Studio {icon('download')}</a></div>'''
